# L §7.6 item 2 (tally 2.1.6, issue #89): with an end from a row, 1..n for n = 1 000 001 is RUN-LIMIT at the ask,
# with step 1 too; step 1000 gives 1 001 keys and answers. tally 2.1.5's refcore answered the first, refused the second
# REFCORE-NOT-YET (its own guard) and answered the third.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input n: int

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n = 1000001 "plan"

ask r: sum(k for k in 1..n)
ask s: sum(k for k in 1..n step 1)
ask t: sum(k for k in 1..n step 1000)
=== expect
r: refused: RUN-LIMIT 1 .. 1 000 001 holds more than 1 000 000 keys
  cut 2026-12-31
s: refused: RUN-LIMIT 1 .. 1 000 001 step 1 holds more than 1 000 000 keys
  cut 2026-12-31
t: 500 501 001
  cut 2026-12-31
